# Posterity — Cursor Rules

## Project
Social media legacy app. Users schedule messages, memories, and videos for delivery to loved ones after account activation. Built by Jeremy Grego (non-technical founder). All code is AI-generated. Full context: read CONTEXT_for_posterity.md in the project root before making any architectural decision.

## Stack
Next.js | Tailwind CSS | Supabase | Stripe | Vercel | GitHub | Twilio | Meta Business API | Buffer | FFmpeg.wasm | Mercury Bank

## Environment
Windows 11, PowerShell. NEVER use && between commands — use semicolons or separate commands.
Node.js v24. Project root: C:\Users\jerth\posterity

## Language Rules — NON-NEGOTIABLE
- ACCOUNTS move through phases. PLANS exist within accounts. Never say "plan phase" or "plan enters Abeyance."
- NEVER use in any customer-facing string, UI label, or copy: death, deceased, passing, died, or any clinical mortality language. Approved terms: "account activation," "trigger event," "after they're gone," "non-response trigger" (internal/comments only).
- Phase names are proper nouns: Horizon, Planning, Abeyance, Active, Twilight, Posterity Phase.

## Six Account Phases (in order)
1. Horizon — building phase, $9.99/year storage fee
2. Planning — account funded, 6-month check-in system active
3. Abeyance — trigger fired, waiting for January 1
4. Active — delivering content per customer calendar (starts January 1)
5. Twilight — final plan year complete, first year free
6. Posterity Phase — trusted contact archive, $9.99/year

## Pricing (LOCKED — do not change without instruction)
Horizon: $9.99/year | Basic: $99/year | Premium: $249/year | Legacy: $899/year
Grace Storage: $4.99/year — admin-assigned only, no public checkout

## Stripe Product Names (use these exact names in Stripe only)
Posterity Horizon | Posterity Basic | Posterity Premium | Posterity Legacy | Posterity Grace

